# Native Settings by touch only (task 014 P2a): a tap on the row under the highlight moves the highlight there, a
# tap on the highlighted row opens it, a drag scrolls and snaps to a row, the header's Esc button goes back one level
# (it calls the page's back action; no key is injected). Review only, no golden.
title settings native touch
review
sizes 480x320 800x480
env APPLAUNCH_SETTINGS_UI native
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 1
apps Settings Store CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
home
header home ZERO
launch Settings
# highlighted row: 480x320 y 158-201 (rows 44), 800x480 y 236-299 (rows 64); Esc button: 253,5 57x30 / 484,8 83x40
@480x320 tap 240 224
@800x480 tap 400 332
shot settings_touch_moved
@480x320 tap 240 180
@800x480 tap 400 268
shot settings_touch_opened
header settings_touch_opened "Settings > Wi-Fi" Wi-Fi
@480x320 drag 240 240 240 180 20
@800x480 drag 400 340 400 255 20
shot settings_touch_dragged
@480x320 tap 281 20
@800x480 tap 525 28
shot settings_touch_esc
header settings_touch_esc Settings
